# mentorOS — Core Rules

These rules apply to every prompt. Never override without explicit user request.

## Project identity

This is **mentorOS** — an AI-native professional cognition operating system.

- **Repo:** mentoros
- **Stack:** Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4, Supabase, Claude API
- **Deployment:** Vercel
- **Design system:** Coda-inspired shell + product-specific accent layers (see `mentoros-design.mdc`)

---

## Folder structure rules

- All source code lives in `src/`
- Routes live in `src/app/`
- Components live in `src/components/`
- Shared logic lives in `src/lib/`
- Custom hooks live in `src/hooks/`
- Types live in `src/types/`
- Static runtime JSON lives in `public/data/`
- Never put components inside `app/` route folders
- Never put business logic inside `page.tsx` files — extract to hooks, lib, or client modules

### PMP module layout (reference implementation)

```
src/components/pmp/
  PMPClient.tsx       — master client state + phase router
  PMPLayout.tsx       — desktop sidebar shell (lg+)
  PMPSidebar.tsx      — left nav
  InputScreen.tsx     — landing / paste / upload
  MoodSelectScreen.tsx
  AnswerPicker.tsx
  AnalyzingScreen.tsx
  result/LessonScreen.tsx
  mood2/Mood2Picker.tsx, Mood2Result.tsx
  shared/             — reusable PMP atoms
src/app/api/pmp/      — analyze, translate, ocr, sessions
src/lib/ai/prompts/pmp.ts
src/types/pmp.ts
```

Use this structure as the template for future product modules (`askbetter`, `nextup`, etc.).

